# Website — consolidated release log

> Reorganized 2026-11-26 under DOCS-RELEASES-TOPIC-REORG-1 (#2974).
> Running history of website changes across
> releases; versions are sections, newest first. Section bodies are
> verbatim from the pre-reorg tree except markdown link targets,
> which were rewritten for the new paths (git history preserves
> the old layout).

## v0.25.12

### EXPL-STATS-1 — explorer-api network-stats: 503 on failed read + anchored_offers rename

`GET /api/analytics/network-stats` no longer answers 200 with a
zero-filled body when the chain database is missing or unreadable — both
failure paths raise HTTP 503 ("chain database unavailable" / "network
stats unavailable") so a failed read can never look like an empty chain.
The success body adds `anchored_offers` (distinct offer keys ever
anchored across GPU_MARKET/GPU_MARKETPLACE/GPU_REGISTER) and keeps
`active_offers` as a deprecated alias with the same value; removal waits
on the website reading the new name (WEB-ANCHORED-1) and docs. Tests
cover the dual-name shape and all three failure cases.


### Website: strict styles, CSP diagnostics and stamped-asset caching

- Move website inline style blocks and attributes into external stylesheets
  and classes. Native hidden state preserves panel visibility; trusted
  CSSOM assignments retain dynamic transaction colors and depth widths.
- Add a bounded same-origin CSP report collector to the Explorer service.
  It validates legacy and Reporting API envelopes and logs sanitized
  diagnostics through the existing logger, excluding URL queries,
  fragments, userinfo, referrers and script samples.
- Prepare nginx rules for strict style-src self and report-uri /csp-report,
  with a 16 KiB body limit and per-client reporting rate limit. Preserve
  the existing HSTS policy and security-header inheritance.
- Cache static JS/CSS carrying the shared 16-hex version stamp for one
  year with immutable. Keep other assets at one hour and HTML no-cache.
  The reference now includes the HTML revalidation rule already live.
- Activation requires the reviewed hub fast-forward, Explorer restart
  and nginx configuration rollout; this entry does not assert deployment.


## v0.25.11

### Website: one canonical main menu on every page (WEB-1)

Each `website/*.html` used to hand-write its own `header-nav` block and
omit the link to itself, so the menu's items and order differed page to
page (Exchange missing on explorer sub-pages, Bridges only on exchange,
dashboards carrying a different set entirely).

- Canonical menu, identical markup on every page that has one:
  Home, Exchange, Explorer, Marketplace, Bridges, Alerts. The page's own
  item stays in place and is marked `class="is-current"
  aria-current="page"` — membership and order never change between pages.
- `customer-dashboard.html` / `shop-dashboard.html` keep the same
  6-item main menu and gain a secondary `dashboard-nav` row
  (Customer Dashboard ↔ Shop Dashboard, own page marked current).
- `follower-api-key-announcement.html` intentionally stays menu-less.
- `website/style.css`: `is-current` is a color-only state (border/text
  `var(--primary)`) — no padding, weight, or width change, so items never
  reflow. `flex-wrap: wrap` keeps the row tidy at phone width.
- `scripts/ops/sync-website-menu.py` stamps the menu between
  `<!-- aitbc-menu:start/end -->` markers (dashboards have their own
  `aitbc-dashboard-menu` pair), is idempotent, and has a `--check` mode
  that fails on drift. To change the menu, edit the `MENU` list in the
  script and re-run it.
- Guard test `tests/unit/test_website_menu_consistency.py` parses every
  page: same items in the same order, exactly one `aria-current="page"`
  pointing at the page's own path (dashboards: in the secondary row;
  pages outside the menu carry none), the allowlist is the only
  menu-less page, and `--check` must be clean.


### Website: page hygiene — landmarks, head metadata, deferred scripts (WEB-2)

- Every page now has a real landmark structure: the main menu is
  `<nav class="header-nav" aria-label="Main">` (inner markup unchanged
  from WEB-1), the dashboards' secondary row is
  `<nav class="dashboard-nav" aria-label="Dashboards">`, and each page's
  primary content sits in `<main id="main" tabindex="-1">`.
- A "Skip to content" link is the first focusable element in <body> on
  every page — including the menu-less announcement page — hidden with
  the clip technique (never display:none) and shown top-left with nav
  tokens + outline on focus. Stamped by the same generator between
  `aitbc-skip` markers.
- Head hygiene: `bridges.html` gains a correct viewport meta (its
  existing tag was a malformed `name="viewport=..."` attribute that
  never applied); titles normalize to "<Page name> — AITBC" everywhere
  except index (kept descriptive per operator); meta descriptions added
  to block, tx, search, and the follower announcement; `<link
  rel="canonical">` on the ten sitemap pages; `noindex` on the dynamic
  block/tx/search pages.
- Every `<script src>` tag is now `defer`red — all site scripts only
  touch the DOM from DOMContentLoaded handlers, so nothing blocks first
  paint and execution order is preserved. No page needed an exception.
- `tests/unit/test_website_menu_consistency.py` gains a hygiene suite:
  viewport/charset/lang, exactly one main and one main nav, skip link
  first, description and title pattern, canonical exactly on sitemap
  pages, noindex exactly on the dynamic pages.



### Website: dashboard init under deferred scripts (WEB-2b)

WEB-2's `defer` on `dashboard.js` broke both dashboard pages: their inline
scripts passed the bare `loadCustomerDashboard` / `loadShopDashboard`
identifier to `addEventListener`, evaluated at parse time before the
deferred file executes — a ReferenceError, so neither dashboard loaded.
WEB-2's own claim ("site scripts only touch the DOM from DOMContentLoaded
handlers") missed the inline listeners.

- `caa30f841` — both pages now wrap the init call in an arrow callback so
  the name resolves when the event fires (the smaller fix vs. moving init
  into `dashboard.js`; the inline script stays the sole init trigger, so
  still exactly one load). Audit of every page's inline `<script>`: only
  these two pages hit; block/tx/search inline blocks are self-contained
  with no external scripts, index's inline block is JSON-LD, the rest
  have no inline JS.
- `caa30f841` — new `tests/unit/test_website_deferred_scripts.py` fails
  any page whose inline script references a name declared top-level in a
  deferred script (or the `lucide`/`Chart` vendor globals) outside a
  callback or function body. Verified: fails with both violations on
  `7e59f6c13`, passes on the fix. Page-load emulation on node2 (`vm`
  contexts replaying parse→defer→DOMContentLoaded order): fixed pages
  init exactly once with no console errors; `7e59f6c13` pages throw
  ReferenceError and never init.



### Website: status strip + site footer (WEB-3)

Every menu page now carries a compact status strip under the header
(static markup, `role="status"`, populated by deferred `status.js`) and
every page including the menu-less announcement page carries an identical
static footer (GitHub mirror, llms.txt, Coordinator API, Explorer API).

- `67850ac59` — new `website/status.js` (no CDN, no vendor): exactly two
  same-origin requests per cycle (`/explorer-api/api/chain/head` +
  `/explorer-api/api/alerts`), jittered >=30s polling, paused while the
  tab is hidden, capped error backoff that stops after repeated failures
  until reload. Head timestamp parsed as UTC (endpoint returns naive
  timestamps); negative age clamped to zero; >60s negative clock skew
  shows height without age; `STALE_AFTER_MS = 300000` switches the label
  `live`/`stale`. Alerts show muted "alerts unknown" when
  `prometheus_ok` is false, `watcher.present` is false, or
  `watcher.stale` is true; the firing count links to `/alerts.html`.
  Fetch failure renders "network status unavailable" — never throws,
  never blocks rendering.
- `67850ac59` — generator `sync-website-menu.py` extended with
  `aitbc-status` / `aitbc-footer` marker regions; still idempotent and
  `--check`-verified. Status strip is stamped as a sibling before
  `<main>` on the 12 menu pages; footer after the container on all 13.
- `67850ac59` — no build line: no public endpoint reports a commit
  (`/explorer-api/health`'s `version: "2.0.0"` is a static app version,
  deliberately not shown). `docs/ops/website-version-json.md` proposes a
  gitignored `website/version.json` written by an operator-installed
  post-merge hook — proposal only, hook install is its own gated task.
- `67850ac59` — `tests/unit/test_website_menu_consistency.py` extended:
  one status strip with `role="status"` on menu pages, `status.js`
  deferred exactly once, identical footer link set on every page, no CDN
  scripts/styles, `status.js` calls only same-origin paths that exist
  under the repo nginx map's location prefixes.

### Website: API path contract test (WEB-4)

New `tests/unit/test_website_api_contract.py` fails loudly when a website
script calls a path that the hub nginx reference config does not expose,
that a location denies (404), or that the proxied app does not implement.

- `3a7337022` — extractor scans website/*.js + inline <script> blocks:
  fetch/EventSource/WebSocket/XHR plus request helpers (apiGet/apiPost/
  apiPostOrGet/fetchJson/getJSON), resolving constants through
  config.js (EXPLORER_API_URL, explorerBase, svc.url object props).
- `3a7337022` — nginx model implements real matching order (exact,
  longest ^~, first regex, longest prefix) over
  examples/nginx/nginx-aitbc.conf.example; AITBC_NGINX_CONF env var
  overrides the config path for live-config drift checks.
- `3a7337022` — app side discovers FastAPI decorators + include_router
  prefixes for coordinator/explorer/rpc/wallet/market/pool-hub/agent-
  coordinator/api-gateway, and parses the exchange's hand-dispatched
  path==/startswith/endswith table. Unmappable upstreams are
  unchecked-app and fail unless allowlisted (allowlist file beside the
  test; stale entries fail too).
- Result on the real tree: 47 path patterns extracted, all ok —
  zero not-exposed / denied / not-implemented / unchecked findings.
  Live-vs-reference location diff (read-only nginx -T): the reference
  is a subset of live; live extras are monitoring/internal (awstats,
  /prom-write, /v1/metrics, plain /agent/).


### test(website): WEB-6 — accessibility + phone-width pass

- Layout/phone: .table-wrap scroll regions (focusable, named) around all
  wide data tables; .endpoint gains overflow-x:auto; 44px minimum tap
  targets for .btn-primary, .copy-btn, .toggle-switch and form controls.
- Focus/keyboard: global :focus-visible outline (--primary, 5.37:1);
  .form-row controls keep a real outline instead of outline:none;
  .toggle-switch input stays keyboard-focusable (clip, not display:none)
  with a focus ring on the slider; click-only cards/rows gain role=link +
  tabindex + Enter activation; deposit/hex copy boxes are role=button with
  Enter/Space handlers.
- Names/labels: aria-label on the previously-unlabeled selects and
  placeholder-only inputs; marketplace toggle labelled; decorative svg
  aria-hidden; ob-banner moved inside <main>; every <table> gets an
  aria-label and every <th> a scope; kv row labels become th[scope=row];
  truncated hashes expose the full value via aria-label/visually-hidden;
  copy actions announce via a polite live region; live feeds announce
  changes (throttled, summary only).
- Contrast/motion (tonal only, same hues): --text-muted #71717a->#83838c
  (4.09/3.86/3.67 -> 5.26/4.96/4.72 on bg/surface/code), --secondary
  #8b5cf6->#a27cf8 (4.40 -> 6.01 on surface); form-control and
  toggle-slider borders move --border -> --text-muted (>=4.7:1);
  .status-sep uses muted; new prefers-reduced-motion block.
- Guard: tests/unit/test_website_a11y.py covers labels, names, headings,
  table semantics, scroll containment, click-handler operability,
  outline rules and reduced-motion (67 violations on the pre-change
  tree, 0 after). Commits: `116a20352`, `c4e06bdb1`, `158b65eed`,
  `1f21a9f4d`, `12cb5c7a5`.


### fix(website): WEB-7 — search page by-address query delimiter (2026-10-15)

- search.html called `/api/blocks/by-address/<addr>&limit=50` — missing
  `?` glued `limit=50` into the address path segment; the explorer
  LIKE-matched nothing, so the address-search blocks section was
  silently always empty. Fixed to `?limit=50`. Live read-only proof:
  buggy URL returns 0 blocks, fixed URL returns the real set.
- Guard: test_website_api_contract.py gains
  test_no_query_delimiter_missing_in_path — any `&` in an extracted
  path pattern fails (red on the buggy tree, green after). No
  assertion weakened; allowlist stays empty.


## v0.25.9

### docs(readme/join): welcome-page README; join docs name the real island

- README is now a welcome page — role diagram, key features, doc pointers — with setup/join/job commands delegated to the docs that carry them (`40ab626`, `737906`).
- The public island is named: join-facing docs carry `hub.aitbc.bubuit.net`, chain `ait-hub.aitbc.bubuit.net`, island `ait-hub.aitbc.bubuit.net-island`, and `http://` (no TLS listener is live — peer keys over `/rpc/join` are cleartext until then). Generic `hub.example.net` uses in API docs and scenarios are unchanged (`020a98`).


### docs(index): hub-page coverage + orphan-docs pre-commit check (2026-09-30)

New `docs/README.md` links every documentation file that had no inbound
link and was worth finding — the ops runbooks, the security set, the
top-level reference pages, the development/reference indexes, and the
component READMEs that sat beside their code. `scripts/docs/
check_orphan_docs.py` now runs in pre-commit: a `.md` file with zero
inbound links fails the commit unless it is in an expected group
(release notes, archive, skills, CI templates, src-adjacent READMEs) or
listed in `scripts/docs/orphan-docs-baseline.txt` — a ratchet baseline
that only shrinks.


### Website — block content breakdown (explorer + latest blocks)

Latest Blocks cards (blocks.html) gain a "Content" row showing the block’s
transaction composition — a thin stacked bar plus colored type chips using
the same per-type palette as the Activity Timeline daily stats
(`TX_TYPE_COLORS` mirrors `analytics.py`). The explorer.html Live Feed
shows the same chips on BLOCK rows. `renderBlockCard` moved to a shared
global in explorer.js — which also fixes a latent ReferenceError when an
address search on explorer.html returned block results (the function was
only defined inside blocks.js scope). Both data sources (`/api/blocks/latest`,
`/api/blocks/non-empty`) already return per-tx `type`; no API change.


